from __future__ import annotations

NAME = "The Art of Doubt"
AMBIENCE = "Gentle Rain"

# A soothing sleep-lecture about the gentle, humble practice of doubt and the patient loop of careful knowing.
SECTIONS = [['You do not have to do anything now but rest.', 'Let the day settle around you like a blanket folding gently over your shoulders.', 'There is nowhere else to be tonight, and nothing left that needs deciding.', 'Feel the weight of your body sink a little further into the bed beneath you.', 'Let your breath slow, soft and easy, in through the nose and out like a quiet tide.', 'You can set down everything you were so sure of today, just for now.', 'All your answers can wait until morning, safe where you left them.', 'Loosen your jaw, let your shoulders drop, let your hands grow heavy and still.', 'There is no question that needs solving in the dark, no problem to carry into sleep.', 'Each breath out lets a little more of the day drift quietly away.', 'You are allowed to simply not know anything at all right now, and to rest in that.', 'Let the quiet hold you, and let yourself grow softer with every slow breath.'], ['Tonight you can think gently about how people come to know things, and find it soothing.', 'To know is a slow and patient thing, and there is no hurry in it.', 'It begins not with certainty but with a small soft wonder, a quiet what if.', 'You notice something, the way you might notice the light change across a wall.', 'You wonder about it, you let a little guess form, light as breath.', 'And then, kindly, you check, you see whether the world agrees with you.', 'This is all that careful knowing really is, a slow loop you can rest inside.', 'Noticing, wondering, guessing, gently testing, and then beginning again.', 'There is no failure in this loop, only a picture growing slowly clearer.', 'You can imagine it turning softly, like a wheel that asks nothing of you.', 'Each turn is patient, each turn is forgiving, each turn is allowed to be wrong.', 'And you can let it turn in the background while you simply lie here and breathe.'], ['To doubt, you may have thought, is a heavy and worried thing.', 'But doubt can be a kindness, a gentle hand held open rather than clenched.', 'To doubt is only to stay curious, to leave a little door ajar.', 'It means you have not closed the question, that you are still listening to the world.', 'There is a softness in saying, perhaps, I am not yet sure.', 'You do not have to grip the truth tightly for it to stay near you.', 'You can hold a question the way you hold a warm cup, loosely, restfully.', 'Being unsure is not the same as being lost, and it need not frighten you.', 'In the spirit of an old teacher who wandered the marketplace asking gentle questions, knowing that you do not know is the very beginning of wisdom.', 'And there is a deep peace in that, a quiet that asks nothing more of you.', 'You can lay down the need to be certain, here in the dark, and feel lighter for it.', 'Let that lightness spread through you as your breath grows slow and long.'], ['Here is the most tender part, and it may surprise you.', 'A careful knower does not try to prove that they are right.', 'They try, with great patience, to prove that they are wrong.', 'They look for the place where their gentle guess might fail, and they welcome it.', 'For if the guess survives every kind attempt to break it, it grows a little stronger.', 'And if it does not survive, then something even better has happened.', 'They have been corrected, and the picture of the world has grown truer.', 'Imagine being glad to be corrected, the way you are glad to be shown a kinder path home.', 'There is no wound in it, only a quiet thank you to the world for teaching you.', 'To be wrong and to notice is not a loss, it is a small gift you give yourself.', 'You can let go of the heavy wish to be right about everything.', 'Let it drift off into the dark, and breathe out slowly as it goes.'], ['You do this gentle testing already, in small homely ways, without naming it.', 'Perhaps you wonder whether the kettle boils faster with its lid set on top.', 'So one evening you simply try it with the lid, and another without, and you watch.', 'You notice, you compare, you let the small truth show itself in its own time.', 'This is the same patient method the great minds use, only smaller and warmer.', 'You might believe a certain window lets in a draft, and one quiet night you check.', 'You hold a candle near it and watch the flame, and the world answers you softly.', 'There is comfort in this, in letting little beliefs be gently tried and trusted or set aside.', 'Nothing has to be settled forever, and nothing has to be perfect.', 'Even the wisest people, in the spirit of those who knew the most, said that the more they learned, the more they saw how little anyone truly knows.', 'They wore that not as a burden but as a kind of grace, an open and humble calm.', 'And so can you, lying here, knowing a little, wondering at the rest, perfectly at ease.'], ['Think of all this knowing as one long, kind conversation with the world.', 'It has been going on for centuries, voice answering voice across the years.', 'No one ever finishes it, and no one is meant to.', 'Each generation listens, adds a gentle word, and passes the question softly on.', 'Science is never truly finished, only ever revising, only ever growing more tender and true.', 'What seems certain today may be lovingly redrawn tomorrow, and that is not a flaw.', 'It is the very thing that keeps the picture alive and breathing.', 'You are part of that long conversation simply by wondering, even half asleep.', 'And you can step out of it whenever you like, to rest, knowing it will keep going without you.', 'The question will still be there in the morning, patient and unhurried.', 'You owe it nothing tonight, no answer, no effort, no certainty at all.', 'You can let the long kind conversation murmur on far away, like soft voices in another room.'], ['Now let every question settle, one by one, like birds folding their wings.', 'There is nothing left to test tonight, nothing to prove, nothing to solve.', 'You can be unsure of everything and completely safe, here in the warm dark.', 'Lay down the wondering, lay down the noticing, lay down even the gentle guessing.', 'The world will keep its mysteries for you, holding them gently until you wake.', 'Feel how light it is to not need to know, to simply rest and breathe.', 'Your thoughts grow slow now, drifting and soft, with no need to follow them.', 'Each breath out carries you a little deeper into quiet.', 'There is no answer you must reach before you sleep, none at all.', 'Let the questions blur, let the wondering dissolve, let it all grow dim and kind.', 'You are safe, you are still, you are allowed to let go of everything now.', 'Rest now, and drift, and sleep.']]
